cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "biodraw: bio-inspired vector drawings for papers, posters and slides"
message: "If you use biodraw in a publication, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Geckt
    given-names: Dean
    email: dgeckt@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/deangeckt/biodraw"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for drawing academic-style cartoon biology — cells,
  dendrites with spines, axons, synapses and wired circuit panels — as clean,
  resolution-independent vector output. Built on numpy and matplotlib only, so
  drawings compose directly with data plots. Shapes are traced from hand
  drawings and normalised into reusable profiles, and every shape can render
  its own construction figure.
keywords:
  - scientific figures
  - visualization
  - matplotlib
  - neuroscience
  - illustration
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev0
